I'm officially onlining a little experiment I've been playing around with
for almost a year now off and on.  The title of the project is StuffCode,
and it's comprised of various magical trinkets like potions, scrolls,
amulets, and rings.

While there are already many of these types of items on EotL, StuffCode is
an entirely new codebase that behaves differently than objects that already
exist out there.  Each StuffCode item is labeled as such in the long
description, however, so you should have no problem telling them apart.  The
system is highly experimental right now, but if it's popular I may try to
implement this system mud-wide and completely replace the other objects.

I'm not going to tell you much except that the system owes most of its
workings to the Nethack model, so if you're familiar with that game you
might recognize some similarities.  Some StuffCode objects will be found in
the same place all the time, but most of them will be randomly dispursed to
room and monsters throughout the mud.  There's some pretty useful items out
there if you look hard enough.

In addition to the random dispersal, I'm reopening Death's old magic store
in Eternal City as The Stuff Outlet Store.  This store will stock various
StuffCode items from time to time, so if you want a sample of what StuffCode
has to offer, that's an easy place to begin looking.

While I'm heading up the Stuff Project, I'm not the sole coder.  In fact,
I've given all the wizards here access to the Stuff directories and they'll
be able to implement their own Stuff creations at will.  For this reason, if
you find any bugs with Stuff objects, your best bet is to report it on the
Player Bug Reports page, since the creator command won't be able to tell you
who coded that particular object.

Some of these objects have already been floating around out there for the
last few months, but I just finished a major overhaul which is why I'm doing
an official release.  As always, constructive feedback is appreciated.  If
you like the Stuff system and have any cool ideas for new Stuff objects, let
me know.

-Devo
